{"term":"circuit","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4f4af855d852ae5204","definition":"The act of moving or revolving around, or as in a circle or orbit; a revolution","example":"After 27 days the moon has made one circuit among the stars, moving from west to east. But in those 27 days the sun has likewise moved eastwardly, about 27 degrees. The moon, then, has to make one circuit and a little more in order to be again in the line joining the earth and sun, in order to be again 'new.'","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arc-fault circuit interrupter","Banana Pancake Circuit","biocircuit","Boolean circuit","chicken-in-a-basket circuit","circuital","circuit bending","circuit board","circuit breaker","circuit-breaker","circuit court","circuit diagram","circuiteer","circuiter","circuit intendant","circuitous","circuit party","circuit queen","circuit race","circuit rank","circuit rider","circuitry","circuit slugger","circuit split","circuit topology","circuit training","circuity","citronella circuit","closed-circuit","closed circuit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circuit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:126242210c843b812a","definition":"The circumference of, or distance around, any space; the measure of a line around an area.","example":"Circuit of the wall from the east to the West","pos":"noun","synonyms":["periplus"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arc-fault circuit interrupter","Banana Pancake Circuit","biocircuit","Boolean circuit","chicken-in-a-basket circuit","circuital","circuit bending","circuit board","circuit breaker","circuit-breaker","circuit court","circuit diagram","circuiteer","circuiter","circuit intendant","circuitous","circuit party","circuit queen","circuit race","circuit rank","circuit rider","circuitry","circuit slugger","circuit split"